      "math_academy_id": "e-5181",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/d3042242136b82b867b8bd7911761ee38318924df0c9979488d20f04117c45d9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf a.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/b316448c885a20a7ed60871ce0f1a4dc4f77bd4658dc6eda3407fb3c89a088cb.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ$, $AH=3$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$ is $\\sqrt{13}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|\\,a\\,|}\\cdot a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}a\\end{aligned}\n$$",
